    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0756" n="642" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg642"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.311D1/79</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McKelvie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-15">June 15, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I am transmitting herewith copy of my
                    report to the Federal Farm Board relative to the World Conference of
                    Wheat-Exporting Nations held in London May 18 to 21 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >23</hi>].</p>
                <pb facs="0757" n="643" xml:id="pg643"/>
                <p>May I suggest that the American Embassy in France will be very glad to have a
                    copy of this? The Embassy in London did not request it but, since Mr. Cox was
                    secretary to the American delegation, I think they would be glad to have it.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Samuel R.
                    McKelvie</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d507-a1.xml" xpointer="d507-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
